-- title:
--   Ordinary unit root at p satisfies α² ≠ 1
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain, complete for its maximal-ideal adic topology and with finite residue field $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$, let $p$ be a prime with $p \ne 2$ and $p \in \mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$, and let $\bar\rho$ be a residual representation over $k$, that is a two-dimensional $k$-space with a multiplicative map $\bar\rho.\rho$ from $\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb Q}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ to its endomorphisms which is trivial on the subgroup fixing some finite extension of $\mathbb Q$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, assumed absolutely irreducible (its base change to $\overline k$ is irreducible). Let $S$ be a finite set of natural numbers, all prime, with $p \in S$, and $N \ge 1$ with $p \nmid N$ and every prime divisor of $N$ in $S$, subject to $\mathrm{HasIntegralStructure}\,N\,2$: the $\mathbb Z$-span of the weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ all of whose $q$-coefficients are rational integers spans the whole space over $\mathbb C$. Let $\theta_0$ be a ring map to $k$ from $\mathrm{heckeAlgebra}\,N\,2\,S$, the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}$ of that space generated by the operators $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$) and $U_q$ ($q$ prime, $q \mid N$, $q \notin S$), such that for every prime $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in which $\ell$ is a non-unit and every $\sigma$ lying in the decomposition subgroup of $P$ and inducing $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$ on the residue field of $P$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho.\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2 - \theta_0(T_\ell)X + \ell$. Let $\pi_{T_0}$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra map to $\mathcal O$ from $\mathrm{heckeLocal}\,N\,S\,\mathcal O\,\theta_0$, the localisation of the $\mathcal O$-base-changed Hecke lattice algebra at the complement of the prime kernel of $\theta_0$, and let $\rho'$ be a two-dimensional adically continuous representation over $\mathcal O$ (a finite free $\mathcal O$-module of rank two) whose Frobenius characteristic polynomials at all such $\ell$ are $X^2 - \pi_{T_0}(\pi(T_\ell))X + \ell$. Finally let $P$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in which $p$ is a non-unit, let $L$ be an $\mathcal O$-submodule of $\rho'.V$ equal to $\mathcal O \cdot b_0$ for some basis $(b_0,b_1)$ of $\rho'.V$, stable under the decomposition subgroup of $P$ over $\mathbb Q$ and with $\rho'.\rho(\sigma)v - v \in L$ for all $v$ and all $\sigma$ in the image in $\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb Q}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ of the inertia subgroup of $P$, and let $\alpha \in \mathcal O$ satisfy $\rho'.\rho(\sigma)v - \alpha v \in L$ for all $v$ and all $\sigma$ in the decomposition subgroup that are Frobenius at $p$ for $P$. Then $\alpha^2 \ne 1$.
--
--   For an ordinary $p$-adic representation attached to a weight-two Hecke eigensystem of level prime to $p$, the scalar by which Frobenius acts on the ordinary line — the unit root of the Frobenius polynomial at $p$ — is not a square root of unity; the classical input is the Eichler–Shimura–Weil bound on $a_p$ together with local–global compatibility at $p$ in Wiles' ordinary theory. The statement supplies the non-vanishing $\alpha^2 - 1 \ne 0$ required by the numerical criterion used in [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.bijective_and_exists_presentation_of_ordinaryCondition_of_finiteAt_of_not_cube_dvd`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.bijective_and_exists_presentation_of_ordinaryCondition_of_finiteAt_of_not_cube_dvd), where the relevant $\eta$-invariant is the ideal generated by $\alpha^2 - 1$.
